request.description:
Liveness, and what the compose healthcheck and the edge probe. Returns {status: "ok", rulesets: [{id, version}, ...] (the compiled versions this copy has cached -- default@2 and the shadow default-llm@1 on this image), bindings: <count>}. A running process has finished startup, which required route-policy-db (migrations + ruleset seeding); /health itself does not touch the database, nor the document classifier. See ROUTE_POLICY.md § API.

#### Schemas

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": ["status", "rulesets", "bindings"],
  "properties": {
    "status": {"const": "ok"},
    "rulesets": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "A ruleset version.",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": ["id", "version"],
        "properties": {
          "id": {"type": "string"},
          "version": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1}
        }
      },
      "description": "The compiled versions this copy has cached"
    },
    "bindings": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "description": "How many bindings it holds"}
  }
}
```

Readiness: a live SELECT 1 on route-policy-db. 200 {status: "ready", db: "up"} when decisions can be logged right now; 503 {status: "not ready", db: "down"} otherwise (the service still DECIDES from its cached rulesets then; only logging stops).

#### Schemas

Response `200` (`application/json`) — decisions can be logged right now:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": ["status", "db"],
  "properties": {
    "status": {"const": "ready"},
    "db": {"const": "up"}
  }
}
```

Response `503` (`application/json`) — route-policy-db did not answer `SELECT 1`; the service still decides from its cached rulesets, only logging stops:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": ["status", "db"],
  "properties": {
    "status": {"const": "not ready"},
    "db": {"const": "down"}
  }
}
```

What a ruleset can contain. evaluator_types: every registered type (regex_text, tool_calls, cooldown, backend_load, static, llm_classifier) with its config JSON schema, whether vote.route is required or the evaluator chooses the route itself (llm_classifier), and its DECLARED output (summary, when it votes, what one exchange's relevance means -- null when it cannot judge single exchanges -- every detail key with its kind, and notes). combiner_types: priority, weighted with their option schemas. roles: vote | force | veto. The declarations live next to each evaluator and are tested against the real code. See ROUTE_POLICY.md § Evaluators.

#### Schemas

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": ["evaluator_types", "combiner_types", "roles"],
  "properties": {
    "evaluator_types": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Every registered evaluator type, by name",
      "additionalProperties": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": ["vote_route", "config_schema", "output"],
        "properties": {
          "vote_route": {"enum": ["required", "chosen by the evaluator"]},
          "config_schema": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": true,
            "description": "A JSON Schema: the type's pydantic config model (model_json_schema())"
          },
          "output": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "The DECLARED output (@declares)",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "required": ["summary", "votes", "relevance", "detail", "notes"],
            "properties": {
              "summary": {"type": "string"},
              "votes": {"type": "string", "description": "When it votes, and for which route"},
              "relevance": {
                "type": ["string", "null"],
                "description": "What one exchange's relevance means; null when the type cannot judge single exchanges"
              },
              "detail": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "Every detail key with its kind",
                "additionalProperties": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "additionalProperties": false,
                  "required": ["kind", "description"],
                  "properties": {
                    "kind": {"enum": ["string", "number", "integer", "boolean", "array", "object"]},
                    "description": {"type": "string"},
                    "nullable": {"const": true},
                    "when": {"type": "string", "description": "Present only in this case"}
                  }
                }
              },
              "notes": {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {"type": "string"}
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "combiner_types": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": ["summary", "config_schema"],
        "properties": {
          "summary": {"type": "string"},
          "config_schema": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": true,
            "description": "A JSON Schema: the type's pydantic config model (model_json_schema())"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "roles": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {"enum": ["vote", "force", "veto", "observe"]}
    }
  }
}
```

