```

Response `200` (`application/json`) — the decision; a repeated decision_id gets the FIRST stored one:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": ["decision_id", "route", "mode", "apply", "ruleset", "votes", "scores", "latency_ms"],
  "properties": {
    "decision_id": {"type": "string", "format": "uuid"},
    "route": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The chain alias. A later call of a `pin: turn` turn gets the turn's first route, unless the fresh decision is local-private"
    },
    "mode": {"enum": ["shadow", "enforce"]},
    "apply": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "True only for an `enforce` ruleset whose invariants held; LiteLLM applies `route` only when it is true"
    },
    "ruleset": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "A ruleset version.",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["id", "version"],
      "properties": {
        "id": {"type": "string"},
        "version": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1}
      }
    },
    "votes": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "One vote, in ruleset order, abstains included.",
        "allOf": [
          {
            "$comment": "The keys every vote carries: a fragment (no type, no additionalProperties) that `vote` and `evaluated_vote` close with unevaluatedProperties: false.",
            "description": "One evaluator's part in a decision. An abstain has `route` and `confidence` null and a reason.",
            "required": [
              "evaluator",
              "type",
              "route",
              "weight",
              "confidence",
              "role",
              "abstained",
              "reason",
              "latency_ms"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "evaluator": {"type": "string", "description": "The evaluator's id in the ruleset"},
              "type": {"type": "string", "description": "Its evaluator type (GET /evaluator-types)"},
              "route": {
                "type": ["string", "null"],
                "description": "The route it voted for; null when it abstained"
              },
              "weight": {"type": "number"},
              "confidence": {"type": ["number", "null"], "description": "Null when it abstained"},
              "role": {"enum": ["vote", "force", "veto", "observe"]},
              "abstained": {"type": "boolean"},
              "reason": {"type": "string"},
              "latency_ms": {"type": "number"}
            },
            "if": {
              "properties": {
                "abstained": {"const": true}
              },
              "required": ["abstained"]
            },
            "then": {
              "properties": {
                "route": {"type": "null"},
                "confidence": {"type": "null"}
              }
            },
            "else": {
              "properties": {
                "route": {"type": "string"},
                "confidence": {"type": "number"}
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "unevaluatedProperties": false
      }
    },
    "scores": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Σ weight × confidence per route, over the non-abstaining `vote` and `force` votes.",
      "additionalProperties": {"type": "number"}
    },
    "latency_ms": {"type": "number"}
  }
}
```

Record what really answered a decided request -- what the hook sends after the call, with the same decision_id. May arrive before or after /decide (no foreign key; the decision_outcomes view joins them). Body: decision_id, litellm_call_id, response_id (the provider's chatcmpl-..., what LiteLLM_SpendLogs.request_id holds), served_model_group (the chain), served_deployment, overflow_reason (busy | down | null), finish_reason, tool_calls (names), status (success | failure), error.

202: {decision_id, stored: true}; stored: false when this decision_id already had an outcome (the first write wins); {decision_id, stored: null, deferred: true} when the write outlasted ROUTE_POLICY_DECISION_WRITE_BUDGET_S and goes on in the background. 422: decision_id not a UUID. 503: the outcome could not be stored (no database, the write failed in time, or too many writes in flight). See ROUTE_POLICY.md § API.

